---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Globalink | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="globalink" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/Glink.svg" alt="Globalink website preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2026</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">Globalink Brand and Website</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A brand identity and website created from scratch for a business that needed a clear digital presence, a flexible CMS, and a professional launch foundation.</p>
      <a href="https://glink.com.co" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external-link">View site <span class="external-link-icon"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.22876 4.22924V5.5586L9.49435 5.56332L3.75736 11.3003L4.70017 12.2431L10.4372 6.50613L10.4324 11.7717H11.7712V4.22924H4.22876Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>Globalink was built as a complete brand and web project. The work covered the initial visual identity, website structure, content organization, and WordPress implementation.</p>
      <p>The project was less about redesigning an existing system and more about creating the first version of a business presence: clear enough to launch, flexible enough to grow, and simple enough for the client to manage.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>Brand direction, website planning, WordPress setup, Elementor implementation, content structure, responsive design, and launch support.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>The business needed to look credible from day one. That meant defining a visual direction, organizing the message, and building a website that could communicate services without feeling generic or unfinished.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Created the brand direction and basic visual system for the website.</li>
        <li>Structured the site around the business offer and the actions visitors needed to take.</li>
        <li>Built the site in WordPress with Elementor for fast iteration and client-friendly editing.</li>
        <li>Designed reusable page sections so future updates could stay consistent.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>The result was a complete launch-ready website with a brand foundation, clear content, and a manageable WordPress setup. It gave the business a professional digital starting point without overcomplicating the system.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
